@SYSTEM_TITLE
; Emuera registers every method as a line-head instruction as well, unless a
; hand-written instruction already owns the name
; (`GameProc/Function/FunctionIdentifier.cs:428-436`), and leaves the value in
; RESULT or RESULTS. The corpus relies on it: `GCREATED 1` and `SPRITECREATED
; "x"` are written as statements.
GCREATE 1, 4, 4
GCREATED 1
PRINTFORML {RESULT}
GCREATED 2
PRINTFORML {RESULT}
; A string-returning method lands in RESULTS.
TOSTR 12
PRINTFORML %RESULTS%
; Arguments are passed positionally, exactly as in the call form.
GWIDTH 1
PRINTFORML {RESULT}
